{"name":"Ceremonial Red Ribbon","hex":"#e63127","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ceremonial","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, relating to, consisting of, or used in a ceremony.","Used only for the purpose of ceremony; symbolic."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A ceremony, or series of ceremonies, prescribed by ritual."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ceremonial"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"},{"term":"ribbon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A long, narrow strip of material used for decoration of clothing or the hair or gift wrapping.","An awareness ribbon."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To decorate with ribbon.","To stripe or streak."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ribbon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Red ribbon","blocks":[{"text":"The red ribbon, as an awareness ribbon, is used as the symbol for the solidarity of people living with HIV/AIDS, and for the awareness and prevention of drug abuse and drunk driving."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Riban_SIDA_a.jpg/330px-Riban_SIDA_a.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_ribbon","wikidata":"Q1139657"},{"title":"Ceremony","blocks":[{"text":"A ceremony is a unified ritualistic event with a purpose, usually consisting of a number of artistic components, performed on a special occasion."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Koninklijk_Koetsier_2013_74.JPG/330px-Koninklijk_Koetsier_2013_74.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ceremony","wikidata":"Q2627975"},{"title":"Ribbon","blocks":[{"text":"A ribbon is a thin band of material, typically cloth but also plastic or sometimes metal, used primarily as decorative binding and tying. Cloth ribbons are made of natural materials such as silk, cotton, and jute and of synthetic materials, such as polyester, nylon, and polypropylene. Ribbon is used for useful, ornamental, and symbolic purposes. Cultures around the world use ribbon in their hair, around the body, and as ornament on non-human animals, buildings, and packaging. Some popular fabrics used to make ribbons are satin, organza, sheer, silk, velvet, and grosgrain."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Scrummy_ribbons_by_Lainey_Powell.jpg/330px-Scrummy_ribbons_by_Lainey_Powell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ribbon","wikidata":"Q6918773"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Jason_Priestley_at_the_44th_Emmy_Awards.jpg/500px-Jason_Priestley_at_the_44th_Emmy_Awards.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Jason_Priestley_at_the_44th_Emmy_Awards.jpg/500px-Jason_Priestley_at_the_44th_Emmy_Awards.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Actor Jason Priestley wearing a red awareness ribbon at the 1992 Emmy Awards","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJason_Priestley_at_the_44th_Emmy_Awards.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/WHredribbonNorthPortico.jpg/500px-WHredribbonNorthPortico.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/WHredribbonNorthPortico.jpg/500px-WHredribbonNorthPortico.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A large red ribbon hangs between columns in the north portico of the White House for World AIDS Day, November 30, 2007.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWHredribbonNorthPortico.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Leaders_welcoming_boy_into_Mexico_Scouting.jpg/500px-Leaders_welcoming_boy_into_Mexico_Scouting.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Leaders_welcoming_boy_into_Mexico_Scouting.jpg/1280px-Leaders_welcoming_boy_into_Mexico_Scouting.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Leaders_welcoming_boy_into_Mexico_Scouting.jpg/500px-Leaders_welcoming_boy_into_Mexico_Scouting.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Leaders welcome a boy into Scouting, March 2010, Mexico City, Mexico.","link":"http